fuxi: 0114 -- look at the screen: kernel-side framebuffer capture over USB

Every claim about the display so far has been a photo held up to a camera, and a
boot that died at the progress bar looks exactly like one that finished. The
console already maps the panel (pe_serial.c probes the "sweet-fbcon" node for
reg/width/height/stride), so the kernel can just read it.

  fb [scale]   decimate by scale (default 4), send the frame to 192.168.7.1:5142
               as "FUXIFB1" + frame/chunk/chunks/width/height/scale/payload and
               RGB triplets, ~1.4 KB per datagram.

pexpert grows fuxi_fbcon_info() because the SecureDT APIs the probe uses are not
exported to bsd/dev. tools/fuxi-fb.py reassembles a frame and writes PNG (PIL when
present) and always a PPM, so the check needs no dependency.

At scale 4 a 1080x2400 panel is 270x600 -- 486 KB, about a thousand datagrams --
which is small enough to pull on demand and large enough to read the progress bar
and the console text.

Harness: applied=113 skipped=0.
